Inertial spin dynamics (TSPIN) examples
=====================================

These inputs demonstrate the TSPIN styles for auxiliary equilibrium sampling
with variable spin magnitudes.  They use a bcc iron lattice with an EAM
potential and independent on-site modulus springs supplied by fix spring/tspin.
They exercise integration and temperature control without an external magnetic
machine-learning potential.  A physical magnetic material model also needs
appropriate magnetic interactions.

  in.spin.tspin       NVE integration with fix nve/tspin.  The conserved
                      energy includes the lattice potential energy, the
                      modulus spring energy, the lattice kinetic energy,
                      and the auxiliary spin kinetic energy.

  in.spin.tspin_nvt   The same system under fix nvt/tspin, which drives the
                      lattice and the spins with two independent Nose-Hoover
                      chains at a common target temperature.

Both inputs require the SPIN and MANYBODY packages and use the included
Fe_mm.eam.fs potential.  Run them from this directory:

  lmp -in in.spin.tspin
  lmp -in in.spin.tspin_nvt

The thermodynamic keyword ke excludes the auxiliary spin kinetic energy.
The inputs report it with compute temp/tspin and include it explicitly in the
variable etot.  That variable is econserve+c_ts[1]: for the isolated NVE input,
econserve equals etotal; for the Nose-Hoover input, it also includes the
thermostat contribution.  The modulus spring energy is included in pe with
fix_modify pin energy yes.

fix langevin/tspin provides an alternative stochastic spin bath when combined
with fix nve/tspin.  It acts only on the spin velocities; temperature control
of the lattice must be specified separately.  That bath does not tally its
energy exchange, so econserve+c_ts[1] is not a conserved energy for this
alternative combination.
